abstract:
Consider a closed manifold $M$ immersed in $\R^m.$ Suppose that the trivial bundle $M	imes\R^m=TM\otimes 
u M$ is equipped with an almost metric connection $	ilde{
abla}$ which almost preserves the decomposition of $M	imes\R^m$ into the tangent and the normal bundle. Assume moreover that the difference $\Gamma=\partial-	ilde{
abla}$ with the usual derivative $\partial$ in $\R^m$ is almost $	ilde{
abla}$-parallel. We show that under these assumptions $M$ admits an extrinsically homogeneous immersion into $\R^m.$
